  <h1>Climbing, skiing, and mountaineering</h1>

  <p>Beyond geology research, my favorite way to explore Earth's landscapes is via climbing. For me, 'climbing' is everything from gym bouldering to Yosemite big walls to Alaskan ridge routes, and it often involves carrying skis on my back. Although this is primarily my academic research website, the two activities are often linked—climbing gets me to the rocks I want to look at. <br /><br />This page is a work in progress, but its aim is to archive both memories and useful information pertaining to new, infrequently repeated, or otherwise noteworthy routes, as well as research-related mountain expeditions. Please contact me for more information regarding any climbs or areas mentioned here.</p>

